Size, macOS: failed run-time checks without their diagnostic strings.

RELEASE_ASSERT and its relatives end in CRASH_WITH_INFO, which hands the
file name and the full C++ signature of the enclosing function to
WTFCrashWithInfo. Every template instantiation has a signature of its own,
and in the Mac port they come to about 4 MiB of text, with the code that
loads it.

With ZEBKIT_TERSE_CRASH_INFO defined, which profiles/macos/slim.xcconfig
does, a failed check stops the process at the same place and says nothing
about where. Linux gets the same from profiles/include/size-prelude.h,
which is put in front of every file there; Xcode's precompiled headers
have to be the first thing included, so that way is closed on macOS.

--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/Assertions.h
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/Assertions.h
@@ -1088,7 +1088,13 @@
 
 // This is useful if you are going to stuff data into registers before crashing, like the
 // crashWithInfo functions below.
-#if !VA_OPT_SUPPORTED
+#if defined(ZEBKIT_TERSE_CRASH_INFO)
+// zebkit: stop at the same place, without the file and signature strings.
+#define CRASH_WITH_INFO(...) do { \
+        WTF::isIntegralOrPointerType(__VA_ARGS__); \
+        CRASH(); \
+    } while (false)
+#elif !VA_OPT_SUPPORTED
 #define CRASH_WITH_INFO(...) do { \
         WTF::isIntegralOrPointerType(__VA_ARGS__); \
         compilerFenceForCrash(); \
